      "content": "That approach makes sense, but I'm worried about the board being sticklers for the technical definitions. Specifically, I need to know how to handle the \"encroachment\" argument if they decide the easement isn't just an inconvenience, but a fundamental violation of the boundary lines. If they view the encroachment as a permanent trespass on the setback zone, what kind of administrative precedents or specific legal arguments can I use to argue for a variance instead of a denial?",
